menu "PM Policy (subsys/pm_policy)"

    config PM_POLICY_MAX_LOCKS
        int "Maximum number of named deep-sleep locks"
        default 8
        range 1 64
        help
            Size of the statically allocated lock table used by
            pm_policy_lock_create(). No dynamic allocation is used, so this bounds
            how many distinct subsystems can each hold a named deep-sleep lock.
            Each entry costs 12 bytes of BSS. Exhaustion fails loudly at init time
            with ESP_ERR_NO_MEM (FW-PMP-003) - a deterministic, immediate failure by
            design (ADR-005).

endmenu
